# 17 Repeat the one-transfer-per-player sensitivity check

## Created

26 November 2026, 14:00:50 Europe/Copenhagen.

## Status

Completed and verified on 26 November 2026. The rerun used 999 transfer selections, as requested, with 999 age-label shuffles per selection.

## Question

How much does the estimated Premier League entry-rate gap change when we vary which eligible transfer represents each player? The [reviewed paper](../paper_output_zip/paper_overleaf_final_no_feeder.zip) reports one draw of 4,602 players, with entry rates of 19.52% for ages 30+ and 21.46% for under 30, a gap of −1.94 percentage points and a one-sided permutation p-value of 0.074. That draw gives a reference point for the repeated analysis.

## Run the check

1. Use the [restricted transfer input](../../reruns/h1_2012_13-2024_25/data/outsideprem_toprem_eligible_transfers.csv.gz) for recorded seasons 2012/13–2024/25 and the [league lookup](../../data/top_five_league_clubs.csv). Reuse the sample builder and permutation procedure in [the H1 producer](../../notebooks/age_shuffle_outsideprem_toprem.py). Verify the input hash against the [manifest](../../reruns/h1_2012_13-2024_25/provenance/reduction_manifest.json), confirm 16,636 eligible transfers from 4,602 players, and reproduce the published fixed-draw result using the original seed and stream ordering. The [saved results](../../reruns/h1_2012_13-2024_25/output/age_shuffle_outsideprem_toprem_results.json) and [prior verification](../../reruns/h1_2012_13-2024_25/provenance/h1_verification.json) give the exact comparison values.
2. Run 999 independently seeded draws. In each draw, sample one eligible transfer uniformly per player, without weighting by age or destination, and derive age group from the selected transfer. Verify each draw contains exactly 4,602 distinct players and both age groups. Hold that set of transfers fixed for 999 age-label shuffles within origin club and recorded season. Keep the older-minus-younger rate gap, lower-tail alternative and plus-one p-value rule from the paper. Record a master seed and use separate random streams for row selection and shuffling.
3. Save a reproducible script, a per-draw CSV and a short summary as new files in the [restricted rerun](../../reruns/h1_2012_13-2024_25/README.md). For each draw, record the two age-group counts and entry rates, the observed gap, the mean shuffled gap and the conditional p-value. Summarise the median and 2.5th–97.5th percentiles of the observed gaps, the fraction of gaps below zero, and how far the observed gap typically falls below or above its own shuffled mean. Compare the original draw with these distributions.

## Completion check

Confirm the original result reproduces, the saved run contains 999 valid draws and the summary regenerates from the CSV. Describe the spread as sensitivity to transfer selection within this fixed set of players. The draws reuse the same players, so report their p-values as conditional diagnostics and give no combined p-value. Keep the saved original outputs and reviewed ZIP intact. Return a short, result-dependent draft for Results and state the draw count and seed for Methods.

