## Verification and findings

- The restricted input and league lookup matched the reduction manifest SHA-256 hashes. The original seed 2026 and stream ordering reproduced the selected rows and all 999 ordered shuffle gaps exactly. Among 16,636 eligible transfers and 4,602 players, the original selection gave entry rates of 19.52% (57/292) at age 30+ and 21.46% (925/4,310) under 30. The exact gap was −1.9411689921495086 percentage points. There were 73 shuffled gaps at or below it, giving p = 0.074.
- Master seed 20261126 generated one child seed per draw and separate selection and permutation streams within each draw. All 999 draws contained the same 4,602 distinct players with both age groups represented. The producer checked the age-group counts in every club–season stratum of all 998,001 repeated-run shuffles. Independent replay matched the observed results for all draws and the shuffle means and lower-tail counts for draws 1, 500 and 999. The summary regenerated from the saved CSV.
- The median older-minus-younger gap was −3.11 percentage points, with central 95% from −5.72 to −0.61. It was negative in 987 of 999 draws (98.8%) and positive in 12. The original gap was at the 81.38th percentile, with 813 draws below it. The size of the gap depended on transfer selection within the fixed set of players, while its direction held in nearly all draws.
- The median observed gap was 1.99 percentage points below its own shuffle mean. The central 95% of observed-minus-shuffle-mean gaps was −4.12 to +0.16 percentage points. The original draw was 2.40 points below its shuffle mean, at the 34.73rd percentile on this scale. The conditional p-values had a median of 0.119 and central 95% from 0.004 to 0.597. The original p-value of 0.074 was at or above 354 of the 999 conditional p-values (35.44%).
- The reviewed manuscript ZIP and the saved H1 outputs matched their pre-run hashes. All 124 files in the original analysis baseline manifest matched their recorded hashes.

## Draft Results

Across 999 repeated selections of one eligible transfer per player, the median older-minus-younger Premier League entry-rate gap was −3.11 percentage points (2.5th–97.5th percentiles, −5.72 to −0.61). The gap was negative in 987 of 999 selections (98.8%), and the original gap of −1.94 percentage points fell at the 81st percentile. The observed gap was typically 1.99 percentage points below its selection-specific shuffle mean.

## Draft Methods

We made 999 independent selections, drawing one eligible transfer uniformly for each of the same 4,602 players and classifying age at the selected transfer. For each selection, we shuffled age labels 999 times within origin club and recorded season, holding destinations and the age-group counts in each stratum fixed. We calculated each conditional lower-tail p-value using the fraction of shuffled gaps at or below the observed older-minus-younger gap, with a plus-one adjustment to the numerator and denominator. A NumPy master seed of 20261126 generated separate random streams for transfer selection and shuffling in each draw.
